{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/undoredo"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoRedo","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add stack-based undo\/redo to your app with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Reference","anchor":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/KeyValueStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"]}],"metadata":{"title":"Undo \/ Redo","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true},{"text":" captures state snapshots before each undoable action. Undo history lives in memory (lost on relaunch), but restored state is persisted normally via ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"restore(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you don’t use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":", nothing changes. It’s fully opt-in.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Adding Undo to Your App","anchor":"Adding-Undo-to-Your-App","level":2},{"text":"1. Create the plugin","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"1-Create-the-plugin"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass declarative predicates to classify which actions are undoable and which coalesce:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let isUndoable: @Sendable (AppAction) -> Bool = { action in","    switch action {","    case .items(.create), .items(.delete), .items(.rename): true","    case .selectItem, .toggleSidebar: false","    }","}","","let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    isUndoable: isUndoable,","    coalescing: { action in","        if case .items(.rename) = action { return true }","        return false","    }",")"]},{"text":"2. Register and pass to Store","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"2-Register-and-pass-to-Store"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register the plugin with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for lifecycle hooks, and pass it directly to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for undo\/redo methods and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canUndo"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canRedo"},{"text":" tracking:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","plugins.register(undoPlugin)","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)","","return Store(","    initialState: AppState(),","    reducer: { state, action in","        reducer.reduce(state: &state, action: action, environment: environment)","    },","    plugins: plugins,","    undoPlugin: undoPlugin,","    persistencePlugin: persistencePlugin,","    isUndoable: isUndoable",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" handles the rest internally: snapshotting state before undoable actions, restoring via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"applyRestore"},{"type":"text","text":" on undo\/redo, draining persistence changes, and updating "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canUndo"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"canRedo"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"3. Wire platform UI","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"3-Wire-platform-UI"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"macOS"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — replace the Edit menu:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["WindowGroup { ... }",".commands {","    CommandGroup(replacing: .undoRedo) {","        Button(\"Undo\") { store.undo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: .command)","            .disabled(!store.canUndo)","        Button(\"Redo\") { store.redo() }","            .keyboardShortcut(\"z\", modifiers: [.command, .shift])","            .disabled(!store.canRedo)","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"iOS","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — bridge the system UndoManager for shake-to-undo:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ In your view — connect the environment UndoManager:",".onAppear { store.undoManager = undoManager }",".onChange(of: undoManager) { _, new in store.undoManager = new }"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically registers undo\/redo actions with the "},{"code":"UndoManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" after each undoable dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Coalescing","anchor":"Coalescing","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"coalescing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" predicate groups consecutive matching actions into a single undo step. The first coalescing action captures a snapshot; subsequent consecutive coalescing actions share that snapshot. A non-coalescing action or undo\/redo resets the flag. Typing “hello” produces one undo entry, not five."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Memory","anchor":"Memory","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each snapshot is a value-type copy of your state. Cost is proportional to the number of entities across all stores. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxDepth"},{"text":" to bound memory for large state:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let undoPlugin = UndoPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(maxDepth: 50, ...)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginAnalyticsReference":{"type":"topic","title":"SwiduxAnalytics Reference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — provider-agnostic analytics with declarative event mapping, auto-identify, and explicit dispatch for the cases the mapper can’t cover."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginanalyticsreference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"type":"topic","title":"EntityStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"type":"topic","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginHost":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PluginHost","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PluginHost","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Ordered registry of plugins that drives the dispatch lifecycle."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginhost","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginHost","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginParentalGateReference":{"type":"topic","title":"SwiduxParentalGate Reference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API surface for the "},{"code":"SwiduxParentalGate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — a domain plugin that guards actions behind a math challenge."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginparentalgatereference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginParentalGateReference","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"type":"topic","title":"Macros","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference for "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — the two macros that generate the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"UndoPlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginKillswitchReference":{"type":"topic","title":"SwiduxKillswitch Reference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Public API surface for the "},{"code":"SwiduxKillswitch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — the plugin, its state and actions, the service abstraction, and the version-comparison primitives."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginkillswitchreference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginKillswitchReference","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Store","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Store","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Generic store that owns the dispatch cycle, plugin lifecycle, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"observation layer."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginFeatureFlagsReference":{"type":"topic","title":"SwiduxFeatureFlags Reference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"API reference for the "},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" library — typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values backed by a Swidux-defined JSON wire format."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginfeatureflagsreference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"type":"topic","title":"Persistence Middleware","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"title":"Getting Started with Swidux","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/KeyValueStoreGuide":{"type":"topic","title":"KeyValueStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist scalar